: "Dana Lee's trip is booked. It went through as two separate bookings because the combined booking only partly worked.\n\n**Booked (both confirmed):**\n- **Flight R0001:** F100, nonstop from SFO to JFK on 2026-11-12, $289. This was the cheapest nonstop. A $199 flight was cheaper but has a stop.\n- **Hotel R0002:** Midtown Lodge (H1) in New York, checking in 2026-11-12 for 2 nights at $189/night, $378 total. This was the cheapest hotel under $250/night.\n- **Total charged to the corporate card:** $667. That's under the $1000 limit, so manager approval wasn't needed.\n\n**What happened:**\n- My combined flight-and-hotel booking timed out. When I retried it, the system said it had failed partway because of an error reserving the hotel.\n- Dana's reservation list showed that the flight had booked and the hotel had not.\n- I then booked the hotel by itself. The final reservation list shows one flight and one hotel, both confirmed, with no duplicates.", "type": "text"}]}]}